            <ArticleTitle>Late in-stent restenosis in a patient with drug-eluting stent.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>648-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Drug coated stents have reduced the incidence of in-stent restenosis with coronary intervention. Whether this effect is long lasting or just delaying the process is not clear. We report here a case of late in-stent restenosis with Rapamycin drug eluting stent.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
